= Vector Spaces and Modules

Vector spaces are the primary structure in linear algebra, generalizing the geometric vectors in the plane and space. Modules satisfy similar axioms but over a ring instead of a field, making them more general but also more complex. Understanding these structures is crucial for various cryptographic algorithms, including those based on lattices and coding theory.

